cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ANIMA (anima-substrate)"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-10-08
authors:
  - alias: Anshul48
    email: anshulraj48@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  ANIMA is designed to plug into the coding tool a developer already
  uses (Muse Code, Claude Code, Codex) and to add a checkable memory
  (TRACE), a State Space Tree screen, voice control and enforced rules.
  Which of those parts exist today is stated in docs/status.json. The
  repository also holds the small,
  offline, stdlib-only Python host for persistent project worlds
  (anima-substrate 0.1.1: nested delegation, pinned participant families,
  crash-atomic local state) and a recorded nine-job run of a hidden
  checker with a tamper-evident decision record. Single-host, toy scale;
  no learning or discovery claims.
keywords:
  - coding-agents
  - agent-memory
  - verification
  - tamper-evident-log
  - offline
license: Apache-2.0
